1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,552
Welcome to Absolute ADAS.

2
00:00:02,902 --> 00:00:10,646
This training walks you through filing and paying our quarterly excise tax return with the Washington State Department of Revenue, also called DOR.

3
00:00:10,995 --> 00:00:15,395
Keep the runbook open while you watch. It has every step as a checklist you can tick off.

4
00:00:16,996 --> 00:00:19,476
Washington doesn't have a state income tax.

5
00:00:19,826 --> 00:00:25,938
Instead, businesses pay B&O tax, which stands for business and occupation, on gross income.

6
00:00:26,288 --> 00:00:30,224
We also send in the retail sales tax we collected from customers.

7
00:00:30,573 --> 00:00:36,077
All of it goes on one combined excise tax return, which we file and pay online in My DOR.

8
00:00:36,427 --> 00:00:42,219
Washington requires businesses to file and pay electronically, so paper returns aren't an option for us.

9
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:47,579
Quarterly returns are due on the last day of the month after the quarter ends.

10
00:00:47,929 --> 00:00:53,641
That's April thirtieth, July thirty-first, October thirty-first, and January thirty-first.

11
00:00:53,991 --> 00:00:58,280
If the due date lands on a weekend or holiday, it moves to the next business day.

12
00:00:58,629 --> 00:01:07,701
For example, the fourth quarter 2026 return is due Monday, February first, 2027, because January thirty-first is a Sunday.

13
00:01:08,051 --> 00:01:13,523
Don't cut it close, though. Our internal target is to have the return filed by the twentieth of the due month.

14
00:01:15,123 --> 00:01:17,507
Before you log in, gather what you need.

15
00:01:17,858 --> 00:01:24,306
First, your own SecureAccess Washington login. The owner adds you as a user on our account. Never share a login.

16
00:01:24,656 --> 00:01:29,359
Second, the sales report for the quarter from Zoho Books, with invoiced totals.

17
00:01:29,710 --> 00:01:34,926
Third, the sales tax we collected, broken out by the location where each job was done.

18
00:01:35,275 --> 00:01:40,331
Fourth, a list of shops we sold to at wholesale. They need a reseller permit on file with us.

19
00:01:40,682 --> 00:01:48,426
And finally, flag any jobs done outside Washington, like our Idaho work. Those are handled differently, so ask before entering them.

20
00:01:50,025 --> 00:01:56,009
Step one. Go to secure.dor.wa.gov and sign in with SecureAccess Washington.

21
00:01:56,359 --> 00:01:58,439
Select the Absolute ADAS account.

22
00:01:58,789 --> 00:02:02,837
Find the open return for the quarter you're filing and click File return.

23
00:02:03,187 --> 00:02:07,283
Double-check the period. Filing the wrong quarter is the most common mistake.

24
00:02:08,883 --> 00:02:12,003
Step two. The return asks which tax lines apply.

25
00:02:12,353 --> 00:02:17,937
Use the same lines we filed last quarter. You can see them on the prior return in My DOR.

26
00:02:18,287 --> 00:02:26,127
Usually that's Retailing B&O plus retail sales tax, and Wholesaling B&O for sales to shops that gave us a reseller permit.

27
00:02:26,477 --> 00:02:31,373
Never add or remove a line on your own. If something looks different, stop and ask.

28
00:02:32,973 --> 00:02:38,653
Step three. For each line, enter the total gross amount for the quarter, straight from the Zoho Books report.

29
00:02:39,003 --> 00:02:44,715
If a deduction applies, such as work done out of state, enter it with the reason DOR asks for.

30
00:02:45,066 --> 00:02:51,098
My DOR calculates the tax for you, and applies the small business credit automatically if we qualify.

31
00:02:52,697 --> 00:02:56,345
Step four. Retail sales tax is reported by location.

32
00:02:56,695 --> 00:03:03,735
Washington is destination-based, so the rate depends on where the work was done, usually the shop's address, not our office.

33
00:03:04,085 --> 00:03:11,269
Each location has a four-digit location code. Look up any you don't recognize with DOR's Tax Rate Lookup tool.

34
00:03:11,619 --> 00:03:15,843
When you're done, the location totals must add up to the retail sales tax line.

35
00:03:17,443 --> 00:03:19,651
Step five. Review before you submit.

36
00:03:20,001 --> 00:03:22,801
Check that every total matches the Zoho Books report.

37
00:03:23,151 --> 00:03:28,863
Then compare against last quarter. If something swings a lot and you can't explain why, stop and ask.

38
00:03:29,213 --> 00:03:33,662
You can save the return and come back later. Nothing is filed until you submit.

39
00:03:34,012 --> 00:03:36,699
Get the owner's sign-off before you move on to payment.

40
00:03:38,299 --> 00:03:39,867
Step six. Pay.

41
00:03:40,217 --> 00:03:45,001
Choose bank account, which is ACH debit. It's free, and it's how we always pay.

42
00:03:45,351 --> 00:03:52,567
Pick a payment date on or before the due date, and make sure the return is submitted by 11:59 p.m. Pacific on the due date.

43
00:03:52,917 --> 00:03:58,117
Don't use a credit or debit card. The processor charges a 2.96% fee.

44
00:03:59,717 --> 00:04:01,493
Step seven. Save your proof.

45
00:04:01,843 --> 00:04:05,876
Write down the confirmation number and download a PDF of the filed return.

46
00:04:06,225 --> 00:04:11,377
Save both to the shared drive, under Taxes, WA DOR, then the year and quarter.

47
00:04:11,728 --> 00:04:16,367
A day or two after the payment date, check the bank account to confirm the debit went through.

48
00:04:17,968 --> 00:04:19,792
Here's why the deadline matters.

49
00:04:20,141 --> 00:04:24,509
If the tax isn't paid by the due date, DOR adds a nine percent penalty.

50
00:04:24,860 --> 00:04:31,548
It jumps to nineteen percent after the end of the following month, and twenty-nine percent after the end of the second month, plus interest.

51
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:36,137
Even in a quarter with no sales, we still have to file a no-business return.

52
00:04:36,487 --> 00:04:40,887
If there's ever a problem paying, file on time anyway and tell the owner right away.

53
00:04:42,487 --> 00:04:43,415
One heads-up.

54
00:04:43,765 --> 00:04:52,069
Starting January first, 2027, the Retailing B&O rate goes up from 0.471% to 0.5%.

55
00:04:52,419 --> 00:05:01,299
That affects the first quarter 2027 return and later. My DOR applies the new rate automatically, so you don't change anything by hand.

56
00:05:02,899 --> 00:05:05,987
Some other quarterly filings are not part of this return.

57
00:05:06,337 --> 00:05:14,241
Employment Security, or ESD, handles unemployment insurance, Paid Family and Medical Leave, and WA Cares.

58
00:05:14,591 --> 00:05:20,655
Labor and Industries handles the workers' comp quarterly report, and federal estimated taxes go to the IRS.

59
00:05:21,005 --> 00:05:24,909
Each one has its own system and deadlines. Those are covered separately.

60
00:05:26,509 --> 00:05:37,149
To recap: gather your numbers, log in, confirm the lines, enter the amounts, report sales tax by location, review, pay by ACH debit, and save your proof.

61
00:05:37,499 --> 00:05:40,603
If anything doesn't look right, ask the owner first.

62
00:05:40,953 --> 00:05:47,033
DOR's taxpayer services line is 360-705-6705.

63
00:05:47,383 --> 00:05:49,655
Thanks for watching, and welcome to the team.
